  "response": "```python\ndef bank_rollback(balance, transactions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply transactions in order to a balance. If any transaction \n    makes the balance negative, reject all and return original balance with False.\n    \n    Args:\n        balance (float or int): Starting account balance\n        transactions (list of numbers): Ordered list of transaction amounts\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: (balance, success) where balance is final if successful, \n               else original; success is True/False\n    \"\"\"\n    current_balance = balance\n    for transaction in transactions:\n        current_balance += transaction\n        if current_balance < 0:\n            return (balance, False)\n    \n    return (current_balance, True)\n```\n\n### Example Usage:\n```python\n# All positive and negative within limits\nprint(bank_rollback(100, [50, -30, -20]))  # Output: (90, True)\n\n# Negative balance occurs on last transaction\nprint(bank_rollback(100, [50, -30, -200]))  # Output: (100, False)\n\n# First transaction causes negative balance\nprint(bank_rollback(100, [-150, 50, -20]))  # Output: (100, False)\n\n# No transactions\nprint(bank_rollback(100, []))  # Output: (100, True)\n\n# Empty balance after all valid transactions\nprint(bank_rollback(0, [100, -100]))  # Output: (0, True)\n\n# Starting with negative balance already\nprint(bank_rollback(-10, [50, -30]))  # Output: (-2, True)\n```",
